data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1465,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb46ebd9c8819180a506ea59bae111","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":37,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"N001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\",\\\"M008\\\",\\\"M009\\\",\\\"M019\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/locals\\\",\\\"value\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact interval [r/2,3r/2]⊂(0,∞)\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Set J=[r/2,3r/2].\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact subset of ℝⁿ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose compact C from H003 for the time window J.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C*\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact nonempty subset of ℝⁿ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Define C*=C∪{0}.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"C\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"K\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"nonnegative real bound for |e_t| on C*×J\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose the nonnegative bound K whose existence is proved as F001 from M019.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"F001\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"C*\\\",\\\"J\\\",\\\"e\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"b\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ℝⁿ→ℝ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Define b(x)=K·1_{C*}(x).\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"K\\\",\\\"C*\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"F\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ℝ→(ℝⁿ→ℝ)\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Define F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ).\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Fprime\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ℝ→(ℝⁿ→ℝ)\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Define Fprime(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ).\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\",\\\"u\\\"]}]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r>0, let J=[r/2,3r/2], and choose compact C from H003 for J. Put C*=C∪{0}, which is compact and nonempty; outside C* we still have u=q throughout J. Thus e_t is continuous on C*×J. By M005, C*×J is compact. Apply M019 to the continuous real function (x,τ)↦|e_t(x,τ)| on this compact set; it is bounded above, so there exists a finite nonnegative K with |e_t(x,τ)|≤K on C*×J; record this existence as F001. Define b(x)=K·1_{C*}(x). Outside C*, e_t=0 by smoothness and constancy of u on the open spatial complement; hence |e_t(x,τ)|≤b(x) for every x and τ∈J. By N001 every compact set has finite Lebesgue measure, so C* is measurable and has finite measure. M008 makes the constant K integrable on C* and M009 makes b integrable on ℝⁿ. Define F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ) and Fprime(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ). Smoothness implies these functions are strongly measurable; N001 gives F(r) integrable, and Fprime(r) strongly measurable. The interval (r/2,3r/2) is a neighborhood of r. The pointwise parameter derivative of F is Fprime by smoothness, and the bound by b holds for every x and every τ in this neighborhood. Thus M006 applies and yields differentiability of E at r with E′(r)=∫e_t(x,r)dx. Since r was arbitrary, the output follows.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/argument/0/produces\\\",\\\"value\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"F001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"There exists a finite real K≥0 such that |e_t(x,τ)|≤K for every (x,τ)∈C*×J.\\\",\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\",\\\"C*\\\",\\\"J\\\"],\\\"assumptions\\\":[]}]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/0/input\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"M005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/0/bindings\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"X=ℝⁿ,Y=[r/2,3r/2], s=C*,t=J.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/0/hypothesis_checks\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"ℝⁿ and the closed interval J are topological spaces.\\\",\\\"C* is compact as the union of compact C and singleton {0}.\\\",\\\"J is compact because it is a closed bounded interval.\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/1/input\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"M006\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/1/bindings\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"α=ℝⁿ,μ=Lebesgue,𝕜=E=ℝ,x₀=r,s=(r/2,3r/2),F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ),F′(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ),bound=b.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/2/input\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"M008\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/3/input\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"M009\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/3/applications/4/input\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"M019\\\"}]}\"}"}

